# L §7.3: pow(x, q) with a non-integer q needs to u. q is a row's value, so the check is the run's, made where the
# value is read, in load's words: RUN-DOMAIN (L §8.4 Load refuses what load sees; tally 2.1.8 §4, #162). 2.1.7's
# refcore printed LOAD-TO at run, refusing the reality.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input two: num
input half: num
def p: num = pow(two, half) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  two = 2
  half = 0.5

ask a: p law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: refused: RUN-DOMAIN pow needs to u
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
